 "structure": "MS (Mississippi College- and Career-Readiness Standards for the Social Studies 2018). This range (pp. 450-481) is the end of the Economics course and the high-school elective courses. Each course has a title table: course title, credit (1 or 1/2 Carnegie credit), 'STRANDS: ...' line, then a two-column table STANDARD | OBJECTIVE(S). Standard codes are course-abbreviation.number (E.6, AWG.1, PAD.1, HAME.1, AAS.1, PSY.1, SOC.1, LRE.1, MIN.1, HUM.1); column C1 holds the standard statement with '(Strands: ...)', C2 (or C3 when split by line) holds the numbered objectives. No grade is given for these courses, so grades=9-12 and course=title as written. The running header 'MISSISSIPPI COLLEGE- and CAREER-READINESS STANDARDS ...' appears as a unit on every page. Economics pages 450-452 are a redline revision with old and new text merged. Page 481 holds closing support-documents text.",
